From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:44:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] windows.web: WebError, reading a failed request the way
 Windows does.

GetStatus turns the HRESULT a web request failed with into a
WebErrorStatus, and the table is Windows' own, measured code by code
over every WinHTTP error and every 0x8019xxxx status: sixteen of the
WinINet/WinHTTP errors (which share their numbers) map, an HTTP status
WebErrorStatus names maps to itself, 0x80190001, 3, 4 and 5 are the
unexpected status, redirection, client and server errors, and
everything else, including a winhttp code under any other facility or
severity, is Unknown.  The statics answer GetRuntimeClassName with
E_ILLEGAL_METHOD_CALL, as a class with only static members does on
Windows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 285c441f1d92cea2901246c8f261da9a495f9351)

